@@ -5,6 +5,27 @@ Run-log events write to the `heartbeat_run_events` table
 Paperclip Telemetry events, and they are not OpenTelemetry exports. A run-log
 event needs no operator endpoint.
 
+## Machine-owned Pi session checkpoint
+
+The `adapter.invoke` event for machine-owned Pi includes `sessionParams` with
+the adapter-selected session path, workspace cwd and remote environment identity.
+Paperclip checkpoints those same parameters before dispatch so an interrupted
+first attempt can retain its session. This records context only; reconnecting
+does not authorize another operation. Session paths contain no credentials, and
+the event stays in the instance run log.
+
+## Plugin run cancellation reconciliation
+
+Providers that advertise `environmentCancelRun` receive the original company and
+run identity. A requested cancellation stays pending until every admitted
+operation has machine termination evidence. If the executor has already ended,
+the scheduler appends a `lifecycle` event with message
+`machine termination reconciled after cancellation` and payload `{ outcome }`.
+The outcome contains exit code, signal, timeout, cancellation or interruption,
+and any bounded supervisor error. It contains no command, credentials or output.
+Natural completion retains its evidenced status. This event stays in the
+instance's run log and does not emit Telemetry or OpenTelemetry data.
+
 ## Native PRP Run-Log Events
 
 The hidden native coordinator writes each validated PRP event to the bound
